// The test-isolation guard (CLAUDE.md "Verify", PRD-01 T17a).
//
// `flushdb` / `flushall` wipe a whole logical database, not the caller's keys.
// Vitest runs test *files* in parallel and Turbo runs *packages* in parallel,
// so a flush anywhere is one suite deleting another suite's in-flight state —
// the exact flake this guard was written after (`@ezpug/bus` losing a queued
// BullMQ job to its neighbour's `beforeEach`).
//
// The replacement is per-package logical databases *and* a per-test-file key
// namespace: `useTestRedis()` hands each file its own `keyPrefix` and cleans up
// with `deleteKeysByPrefix`, so a suite can only ever destroy its own state.
//
// Escape hatch, for a genuine exception (a one-shot ops script owning the
// whole server):
//
//   // biome-ignore lint/plugin: <why this may wipe the database>

language js

`$client.$member($...)` where {
  $member <: or { "flushdb", "flushall" },
  register_diagnostic(
    span = $member,
    message = "Test isolation: never flush a whole Redis database — suites run in parallel and share it. Delete your own namespace instead (`deleteKeysByPrefix(client, keyPrefix)` from the package's `redis-testing.ts`). Suppress with `// biome-ignore lint/plugin: <reason>` if this really owns the server.",
    severity = "error",
  )
}
